# Diagnostics-First Development

Every feature must be fully observable through the existing `Diagnostics` system so that a single "Copy diagnostics" blob is enough context to diagnose and fix any failure.

## Rule: Instrument all meaningful states

For every new code path, call the appropriate helper from `extension/src/background/diagnostics.ts`:

| Situation | Call |
|---|---|
| New per-symbol/source job starts | `seedJob(source, symbol, url)` |
| Job state changes | `updateJob(source, symbol, { status, message?, dataSummary?, data?, debug? })` |
| Unrecoverable / unexpected error | `addError(where, message)` — `where` = function/feature name |
| New top-level settings or config loaded | `setMeta({ settings })` |
| New Realtime subscription added | mirror `setScrapeRequestsWatching` / `setAnalysisRequestsWatching` pattern |

## Rule: `debug` must capture the decision inputs

When a scrape or parse produces a wrong result (empty, stale, misparse), the root cause is almost always the DOM state or raw API response at that moment. Always attach a `debug` object to `updateJob`:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — impossible to diagnose from a copy
updateJob(source, symbol, { status: "empty" });

// ✅ GOOD — debug tells you exactly what the selector saw
updateJob(source, symbol, {
  status: "empty",
  message: "bid selector returned null",
  debug: {
    selectorTried: ".bid-price",
    outerHTML: el?.outerHTML ?? null,
    pageTitle: document.title,
    url: location.href,
  },
});
```

## Rule: `message` must be a complete sentence

`message` and the `where`/`message` pair in `addError` are shown verbatim in the copy blob. Write them so they are actionable without reading code:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
addError("scrape", "failed");

// ✅ GOOD
addError("scrapeCore.persistWrite", `Supabase upsert rejected: ${err.message} (code ${err.code})`);
```

## Rule: `dataSummary` for every successful scrape

Successful jobs should include a one-line human summary so it's easy to confirm the right data was captured:

```typescript
updateJob(source, symbol, {
  status: "scraped",
  dataSummary: `bid=${write.bid} ask=${write.ask} iv=${write.iv} rows=${write.chains?.length ?? 0}`,
  data: write,
});
```

## Rule: New request-trigger paths get their own `RequestsIndicator`

If you add a new Supabase Realtime subscription (a new table trigger), follow the `scrapeRequests` / `analysisRequests` pattern in `diagnostics.ts`:
- Add a typed indicator to `Diagnostics` in `contracts/src/diagnostics.ts`
- Track `watching`, `subStatus`, `received`, `lastEventAt`, `lastRequestId`, `lastCheckedAt`
- Include it in `formatDiagnostics` so it appears in the copy blob

## What the copy blob must answer

Before shipping a feature ask: "If this silently fails at 3 AM, can I paste the diagnostics blob here and immediately know **what** ran, **what** it saw, and **why** it stopped?" If the answer is no, add more instrumentation.
